Part 1 – Document Indexing & Retrieval Build a Python module that receives a PDF or DOCX file, extracts clean text, splits it into chunks, creates embeddings using the Gemini API, stores the data in PostgreSQL with pgvector, and supports semantic search over the stored content. Mandatory requirements • Create an indexing script named index_documents.py that receives a PDF/DOCX file through a simple terminal command. • Extract clean text and handle unsupported files or documents with no extractable text. • Implement three chunking strategies: fixed-size with overlap, sentence-based splitting, and paragraphbased splitting. • Generate embeddings using gemini-embedding-001 and store them in PostgreSQL using pgvector. • The table should include at least: id, chunk_text, embedding, filename, split_strategy, created_at. • Implement semantic search using vector similarity search, for example with search.py or another CLI command. • Use a .env file for GEMINI_API_KEY and POSTGRES_URL. Do not store API keys or connection details in the code. Example commands python index_documents.py --file ./docs/example.pdf --strategy paragraph python search.py --query "login issue" Error handling Handle at least: missing file, unsupported file type, document with no text, embedding failure, database connection failure, and empty search results. Submission requirements • GitHub link containing the full code, requirements.txt, and a README.md in English with installation instructions, environment variables, run examples, and sample output. • Include an example indexing run, an example search run, and example search results returned from the database. • Code should be clean, modular, documented, without hardcoded file paths, and without printing secrets or API keys. 